// The generator round on {3,4,3,4} as right multiplication by a Coxeter element, exactly. Algebra: spin-one.
//
// THE MODEL. The tiles of the {3,4,3,4} honeycomb are the elements of the right-angled Coxeter group W generated by the
// 24 facet reflections s_0 .. s_23 of the right-angled 24-cell (s_g s_h = s_h s_g when facets g and h meet, infinite
// order otherwise), and color g pairs tile x with x s_g (code/compute/lab/lazy-space.ts rightAngledSpace). That this
// Cayley graph is the geometric tile graph is Poincare's polyhedron theorem, taken as the model here, not proved. A
// round applies the colors in index order (forward) or reversed, so a tone that crosses every matching of a round
// moves from x to x w, where w = s_0 s_1 ... s_23 is the round's Coxeter element (x w^-1 under the reversed order).
// In the faithful representation the s_g are the facet reflections F_g of code/substrate/coxeter/exact-3434.ts, 5 x 5
// matrices over Z[sqrt 2] preserving the Lorentz form 2B, so w, its powers and every conjugate of a reflection are
// exact integer matrices, compared entry for entry.
//
// THE READINGS, fixed before the first run:
//   R1  every rule cell: each of the 24 conservative reversible pair rules (code/rule/pair-rule.ts), on each uniform
//       background b it fixes, with each lone tone x != b, under both color orders, started on every tile of the
//       radius-2 ball (481 tiles), read at the ends of rounds 1..ROUNDS (8). A start reads frozen (it never leaves its
//       tile), translated (its tile after round t is x w^t), counter-translated (x w^-t), moving (one tone, any other
//       track) or other (the support leaves one cell). A cell is frozen, translated or counter-translated when every
//       start reads so, orientation-dependent when every start keeps one tone but the starts disagree or move
//       otherwise (the orientation, shorter tile first, is word length, which no left translation preserves), and
//       other otherwise. Creating rules (the vacuum pair (0, 0) moves) are not read on the vacuum: their background is
//       live. The PREDICTION from the table alone: the cell of tone x on background b is orientation-blind exactly when
//       the rule fixes both (x, b) and (b, x) (frozen) or exchanges them (translated); every other cell keeps one tone
//       only if one of the two pairs stays a lone tone.
//   R2  the mirrors: the reflections a tone crosses inside round 1 are r_k = P_k s_k P_k^-1 (P_k the product of the
//       first k letters of the round), and inside round t the conjugates w^(t-1) r_k w^-(t-1). Every conjugate for
//       t = 0..MIRROR_POWERS (64) is computed exactly, and every coincidence of two of them is listed: w^d r_k w^-d
//       = r_k' for some d >= 1 is a w-invariant mirror family (w r w^-1 = r for d = 1, k = k').
//   R3  meetings: two translated tones at x and y are paired at color k of round t exactly when y = x C with
//       C = w^(t-1) r_k w^-(t-1). Left multiplication commutes with right multiplication by every s_g, so the pairs
//       (x, y) and (1, x^-1 y) meet at the same matchings, and x = 1 covers every pair. For every y in the radius-3
//       ball (8,856 tiles besides the origin) the rounds 1..MEET_ROUNDS (64) at which (1, y) is paired are counted by
//       matrix lookup, and checked by stepping two free movers on the lazy tiling for every y of the radius-2 ball and
//       for one off-origin anchor. Free movers ignore the rule at the meeting itself: this counts encounters, which is
//       what a finite-interaction argument bounds.
//   CONTROL D4  the flat partner {3,4,3,3} on the D4 lattice under its step-parity coloring (lazy-space.ts
//       latticeSpace, 24 colors, color 2k + e pairs x with x + r_k where the parity coordinate of x is e). The same R1
//       reading, with "translated" meaning a constant displacement per round (the round is a lattice translation on
//       each parity class), and the same meeting count for every pair within distance 3 of the 25 tiles of the radius-1
//       ball. Prediction: pairs whose relative position the round preserves meet in every round (wrong, see FIRST RUN).
//   CONTROL LEVEL 4  W reduced modulo (sqrt 2)^4 = (4) (congruence-3434.ts levelRing): the finite Cayley graph of the
//       image of W, colors by right multiplication, orientation the lower dock index first. There w has finite order
//       (reported), so the meeting count must recur: the finite-meeting statement must fail on it.
//
// GATES, each able to fail: the census finds 24 rules; F_g^2 = 1 and F_g preserves 2B for every g; F_g F_h = F_h F_g
// exactly when the lazy tiling's Coxeter matrix says m = 2, and 2B(n_g, n_h) <= -2 (an infinite dihedral pair) when it
// says infinity; w preserves 2B, has trace > 5 (loxodromic, so of infinite order) and w^t != 1 for t <= MIRROR_POWERS;
// every conjugate C is a reflection (C^2 = 1, C != 1); every predicted orientation-blind cell reads its predicted
// class from every start on {3,4,3,4}, on the level-4 quotient and (frozen or a constant translation) on D4; the
// matrix count and the stepped count agree on every y of the radius-2 ball; the off-origin anchor reads the same
// counts; the quotient's generators are distinct involutions with no fixed dock. Verdict: fail if a gate fails,
// pass otherwise, with every reading reported as measured.
//
// FIRST RUN, 2026-11-28 (tmp/coxeter-round.log, 38 s): fail on one gate, the quotient's blind cells. Modulo
// (sqrt 2)^4 the Coxeter element is the identity (order 1), so a translated tone is back on its dock at every round
// end and reads frozen there: round ends cannot tell x w^t from x when w = 1. The gate now accepts 'frozen' for a
// predicted translated cell exactly when the quotient's w has order 1, and says so. The D4 prediction above was wrong:
// two free movers that are paired exchange tiles, so their difference flips sign, and partners differ by a root, which
// puts them in different parity classes with different round displacements: on D4 too every near pair is paired at
// most once. So finitely many meetings is NOT what separates the hyperbolic round from the flat one: the flat round is
// a translation per parity class and meets finitely just the same. What does differ is the quotient, where w = 1 makes
// 48 pairs meet in every round.
//
// DETERMINISM: every start, pair and power is enumerated, in canonical order. No random number anywhere. Depth L1:
// exact readings of the model's own round, with matched flat and finite controls.

import { HarnessRule, fixesBackground, harnessRule, lazySpaceFactory } from '@/code/compute/lab/harness'
import { LazyRun, LazySpace, roundColors, spaceBall } from '@/code/compute/lab/lazy-space'
import { pairIndex, pairRuleCensus } from '@/code/rule/pair-rule'
import { levelRing, reduceToLevel, type LevelRing } from '@/code/substrate/coxeter/congruence-3434'
import {
  TWICE_GRAM,
  exactCell,
  matrixProduct,
  twiceForm,
  type ExactMatrix,
} from '@/code/substrate/coxeter/exact-3434'
import { tilingSystem } from '@/code/substrate/coxeter/chamber-tiling'
import { experiment } from '@/test/scaffold/suite'
import { verdict } from '@/test/scaffold/verdict'

const ROUNDS = 8
const MIRROR_POWERS = 64
const MEET_ROUNDS = 64
const START_RADIUS = 2
const MEET_RADIUS = 3
const CHECK_RADIUS = 2
const LEVEL_TWO_POWER = 4
const QUOTIENT_CAP = 400_000
const SUPPORT_CAP = 64
const DIM = 5
const BACKGROUNDS = [-1, 0, 1] as const

type Order = 'forward' | 'reverse'

const ORDERS: readonly Order[] = ['forward', 'reverse']

// ---- exact Z[sqrt 2] matrices ----

const key = (m: ExactMatrix): string => m.join(',')

function identity(): ExactMatrix {
  const m = new Array<bigint>(2 * DIM * DIM).fill(0n)

  for (let i = 0; i < DIM; i++) {
    m[2 * (i * DIM + i)] = 1n
  }

  return m
}

const IDENTITY_KEY = key(identity())

function transpose(m: ExactMatrix): ExactMatrix {
  const out = new Array<bigint>(2 * DIM * DIM)

  for (let i = 0; i < DIM; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < DIM; j++) {
      out[2 * (j * DIM + i)] = m[2 * (i * DIM + j)]!
      out[2 * (j * DIM + i) + 1] = m[2 * (i * DIM + j) + 1]!
    }
  }

  return out
}

const product = (letters: readonly ExactMatrix[]): ExactMatrix =>
  letters.reduce((acc, m) => matrixProduct(acc, m), identity())

const preservesForm = (m: ExactMatrix): boolean =>
  key(matrixProduct(matrixProduct(transpose(m), TWICE_GRAM), m)) === key(TWICE_GRAM)

// the sign of a + b sqrt 2, exactly
function sqrtTwoSign(a: bigint, b: bigint): number {
  if (a >= 0n && b >= 0n) {
    return a === 0n && b === 0n ? 0 : 1
  }

  if (a <= 0n && b <= 0n) {
    return -1
  }

  const d = a * a - 2n * b * b

  return a > 0n ? (d > 0n ? 1 : -1) : d > 0n ? -1 : 1
}

function trace(m: ExactMatrix): [bigint, bigint] {
  let a = 0n
  let b = 0n

  for (let i = 0; i < DIM; i++) {
    a += m[2 * (i * DIM + i)]!
    b += m[2 * (i * DIM + i) + 1]!
  }

  return [a, b]
}

// ---- the round's letters ----

const roundLetters = (order: Order): number[] => {
  const forward = Array.from({ length: 24 }, (_, g) => g)

  return order === 'forward' ? forward : forward.reverse()
}

type RoundAlgebra = {
  order: Order
  w: ExactMatrix
  wInverse: ExactMatrix
  // conjugates[t][k] = w^t r_k w^-t, t = 0..MIRROR_POWERS
  conjugates: ExactMatrix[][]
  powers: ExactMatrix[]
}

function roundAlgebra(faces: readonly ExactMatrix[], order: Order): RoundAlgebra {
  const letters = roundLetters(order)
  const w = product(letters.map(g => faces[g]!))
  const wInverse = product([...letters].reverse().map(g => faces[g]!))
  const mirrors = letters.map((g, k) => {
    const prefix = product(letters.slice(0, k).map(h => faces[h]!))
    const prefixInverse = product(letters.slice(0, k).reverse().map(h => faces[h]!))

    return matrixProduct(matrixProduct(prefix, faces[g]!), prefixInverse)
  })
  const powers: ExactMatrix[] = [identity()]
  const inversePowers: ExactMatrix[] = [identity()]

  for (let t = 1; t <= MIRROR_POWERS; t++) {
    powers.push(matrixProduct(powers[t - 1]!, w))
    inversePowers.push(matrixProduct(wInverse, inversePowers[t - 1]!))
  }

  const conjugates = powers.map((p, t) =>
    mirrors.map(r => matrixProduct(matrixProduct(p, r), inversePowers[t]!)),
  )

  return { order, w, wInverse, conjugates, powers }
}

// ---- lone-tone readings on any lazy space ----

type StartClass = 'frozen' | 'translated' | 'counter' | 'moving' | 'other'
type CellClass = 'frozen' | 'translated' | 'counter' | 'orientation-dependent' | 'other' | 'live background'

// the class the table alone predicts for tone x on background b, or null when the cell is not orientation-blind
function predictedClass(rule: HarnessRule, x: number, b: number): 'frozen' | 'translated' | null {
  const p = pairIndex(x, b)
  const q = pairIndex(b, x)

  if (rule.table[p] === p && rule.table[q] === q) {
    return 'frozen'
  }

  if (rule.table[p] === q && rule.table[q] === p) {
    return 'translated'
  }

  return null
}

type Track = (start: number, t: number) => number

// One lone-tone run: its class against the expected tracks (null for a space where translation is read by
// displacement instead).
function readStart(input: {
  space: LazySpace
  rule: HarnessRule
  background: number
  tone: number
  order: Order
  start: number
  along: Track | null
  against: Track | null
  displacement: ((a: number, b: number) => string) | null
}): StartClass {
  const run = new LazyRun({
    space: input.space,
    background: input.background,
    colors: roundColors(input.space, input.order),
    supportCap: SUPPORT_CAP,
  })

  run.set(input.start, input.tone)

  const cells: number[] = [input.start]

  for (let t = 1; t <= ROUNDS; t++) {
    if (!run.round(input.rule) || run.state.size !== 1) {
      return 'other'
    }

    const [cell] = run.state.keys()

    if (run.state.get(cell!) !== input.tone) {
      return 'other'
    }

    cells.push(cell!)
  }

  if (cells.every(c => c === input.start)) {
    return 'frozen'
  }

  if (input.along && cells.every((c, t) => c === input.along!(input.start, t))) {
    return 'translated'
  }

  if (input.against && cells.every((c, t) => c === input.against!(input.start, t))) {
    return 'counter'
  }

  if (input.displacement) {
    const steps = cells.slice(1).map((c, t) => input.displacement!(cells[t]!, c))

    if (steps.every(s => s === steps[0])) {
      return 'translated'
    }
  }

  return 'moving'
}

function cellClass(classes: readonly StartClass[]): CellClass {
  const first = classes[0]!

  if (first !== 'moving' && first !== 'other' && classes.every(c => c === first)) {
    return first
  }

  return classes.every(c => c !== 'other') ? 'orientation-dependent' : 'other'
}

type CellReading = {
  rule: string
  background: number
  tone: number
  order: Order
  predicted: 'frozen' | 'translated' | null
  read: CellClass
  // for a translated or counter-translated cell, the expected class under its order
  agrees: boolean
}

function readCells(input: {
  space: LazySpace
  rules: readonly HarnessRule[]
  starts: readonly number[]
  tracks: (order: Order) => { along: Track | null; against: Track | null }
  displacement: ((a: number, b: number) => string) | null
}): CellReading[] {
  const out: CellReading[] = []

  for (const rule of input.rules) {
    for (const background of BACKGROUNDS) {
      for (const tone of [-1, 0, 1].filter(x => x !== background)) {
        for (const order of ORDERS) {
          const predicted = predictedClass(rule, tone, background)

          if (!fixesBackground(rule, background)) {
            out.push({ rule: rule.name, background, tone, order, predicted, read: 'live background', agrees: true })
            continue
          }

          const { along, against } = input.tracks(order)
          const classes = input.starts.map(start =>
            readStart({
              space: input.space,
              rule,
              background,
              tone,
              order,
              start,
              along,
              against,
              displacement: input.displacement,
            }),
          )
          const read = cellClass(classes)
          // under the generator schedule a translated cell moves by the round's own element: x w forward, x w^-1
          // reversed, and w^-1 is the reversed round's element, so 'translated' is the expected reading under both
          const agrees =
            predicted === null
              ? read !== 'frozen' && read !== 'translated' && read !== 'counter'
              : predicted === read

          out.push({ rule: rule.name, background, tone, order, predicted, read, agrees })
        }
      }
    }
  }

  return out
}

// ---- the level-4 quotient of W ----

type Quotient = {
  ring: LevelRing
  fits: boolean
  docks: number
  // docks * 24
  table: Int32Array
  distance: Int32Array
  indexOf: Map<string, number>
}

function levelProduct(g: Int32Array, t: Int32Array, ring: LevelRing): Int32Array {
  const out = new Int32Array(2 * DIM * DIM)
  const E = DIM * DIM

  for (let i = 0; i < DIM; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < DIM; j++) {
      let sa = 0
      let sb = 0

      for (let l = 0; l < DIM; l++) {
        const ga = g[i * DIM + l]!
        const gb = g[E + i * DIM + l]!
        const ta = t[l * DIM + j]!
        const tb = t[E + l * DIM + j]!

        sa += ga * ta + 2 * gb * tb
        sb += ga * tb + gb * ta
      }

      out[i * DIM + j] = sa % ring.modA
      out[E + i * DIM + j] = sb % ring.modB
    }
  }

  return out
}

function quotientOfW(faces: readonly ExactMatrix[], ring: LevelRing): Quotient {
  const letters = faces.map(f => reduceToLevel(f, ring))
  const one = reduceToLevel(identity(), ring)
  const indexOf = new Map<string, number>([[one.join(','), 0]])
  const frames: Int32Array[] = [one]
  const table: number[] = []
  const distance: number[] = [0]

  for (let head = 0; head < frames.length; head++) {
    for (let g = 0; g < 24; g++) {
      const next = levelProduct(frames[head]!, letters[g]!, ring)
      const k = next.join(',')

      let id = indexOf.get(k)

      if (id === undefined) {
        if (frames.length >= QUOTIENT_CAP) {
          return { ring, fits: false, docks: frames.length, table: new Int32Array(0), distance: new Int32Array(0), indexOf }
        }

        id = frames.length
        indexOf.set(k, id)
        frames.push(next)
        distance.push(distance[head]! + 1)
      }

      table.push(id)
    }
  }

  return {
    ring,
    fits: true,
    docks: frames.length,
    table: Int32Array.from(table),
    distance: Int32Array.from(distance),
    indexOf,
  }
}

function quotientSpace(q: Quotient): LazySpace {
  const unused = (what: string): never => {
    throw new Error(`coxeter-round-3434: the quotient space has no ${what}`)
  }

  return {
    name: `{3,4,3,4} mod ${q.ring.name}`,
    degree: 24,
    colorCount: 24,
    coloring: 'generator coloring of W mod (sqrt 2)^4 (color g pairs x with x s_g)',
    orientation: 'the lower dock index (breadth-first from the identity) first',
    cells: () => q.docks,
    distance: c => q.distance[c]!,
    distanceBetween: () => unused('distanceBetween'),
    neighbors: c => Array.from({ length: 24 }, (_, g) => q.table[c * 24 + g]!),
    partner: (g, c) => q.table[c * 24 + g]!,
    isFirst: (g, c) => c < q.table[c * 24 + g]!,
    compare: (a, b) => a - b,
    ballSize: () => unused('ballSize'),
    address: c => String(c),
    fromAddress: a => Number(a),
  }
}

// ---- free movers ----

// the rounds 1..MEET_ROUNDS at which free movers started at a and b are paired, stepped on the space
function steppedMeetings(space: LazySpace, a0: number, b0: number, order: Order): number[] {
  const colors = roundColors(space, order)
  const rounds: number[] = []

  let a = a0
  let b = b0

  for (let t = 1; t <= MEET_ROUNDS; t++) {
    let met = false

    for (const g of colors) {
      const pa = space.partner(g, a)

      if (pa === b) {
        met = true
      }

      b = space.partner(g, b)
      a = pa
    }

    if (met) {
      rounds.push(t)
    }
  }

  return rounds
}

// the rounds at which (1, y) is paired, by matrix lookup: round t holds the conjugates w^(t-1) r_k w^-(t-1)
function matrixMeetings(algebra: RoundAlgebra): Map<string, number[]> {
  const byKey = new Map<string, number[]>()

  for (let t = 1; t <= MEET_ROUNDS; t++) {
    for (const c of algebra.conjugates[t - 1]!) {
      const k = key(c)
      const list = byKey.get(k) ?? []

      if (list[list.length - 1] !== t) {
        list.push(t)
      }

      byKey.set(k, list)
    }
  }

  return byKey
}

function histogram(counts: readonly number[]): string {
  const h = new Map<number, number>()

  for (const c of counts) {
    h.set(c, (h.get(c) ?? 0) + 1)
  }

  return [...h.entries()]
    .sort((x, y) => x[0] - y[0])
    .map(([c, n]) => `${c}:${n}`)
    .join(' ')
}

export default experiment({
  id: 'computation/coxeter-round-3434',
  code: 'E-CMP-0099',
  title:
    'the generator round on {3,4,3,4} is right multiplication by a Coxeter element of infinite order: every orientation-blind lone tone is frozen or moves x -> x w, and two translated tones meet only at conjugates of the round mirrors, against the flat D4 lattice (a translation) and the level-4 quotient (w of finite order)',
  category: 'computation',
  substrates: 'any',
  depth: 'L1',
  paper: false,
  run() {
    const census = pairRuleCensus()
    const rules = census.rules.map(r => harnessRule({ name: r.name, table: r.table }))
    const cell = exactCell()
    const faces = cell.faces
    const system = tilingSystem([3, 4, 3, 4], 'tile')!
    const coxeter = system.coxeter

    // ---- gates on the representation ----
    const involutions = faces.every(f => key(matrixProduct(f, f)) === IDENTITY_KEY)
    const facesPreserve = faces.every(preservesForm)

    let commutationAgrees = true
    let infinitePairsAgree = true

    for (let g = 0; g < 24; g++) {
      for (let h = g + 1; h < 24; h++) {
        const commute = key(matrixProduct(faces[g]!, faces[h]!)) === key(matrixProduct(faces[h]!, faces[g]!))
        const [a, b] = twiceForm(cell.normals[cell.faceOfLabel[g]!]!, cell.normals[cell.faceOfLabel[h]!]!)

        if (commute !== (coxeter[g]![h] === 2)) {
          commutationAgrees = false
        }

        if (coxeter[g]![h] === 2 ? a !== 0n || b !== 0n : sqrtTwoSign(a + 2n, b) > 0) {
          infinitePairsAgree = false
        }
      }
    }

    const algebras = ORDERS.map(order => roundAlgebra(faces, order))
    const forward = algebras[0]!
    const wTrace = trace(forward.w)
    const loxodromic = sqrtTwoSign(wTrace[0] - 5n, wTrace[1]) > 0
    const wPreserves = preservesForm(forward.w)
    const wInverseAgrees = key(algebras[1]!.w) === key(forward.wInverse)
    const noPowerIsOne = forward.powers.slice(1).every(p => key(p) !== IDENTITY_KEY)
    const conjugatesAreReflections = algebras.every(al =>
      al.conjugates.every(row => row.every(c => key(c) !== IDENTITY_KEY && key(matrixProduct(c, c)) === IDENTITY_KEY)),
    )

    // ---- R2: coincident mirror conjugates ----
    const mirrorRepeats: string[] = []

    let invariantMirrors = 0

    for (const al of algebras) {
      const seen = new Map<string, [number, number]>()

      al.conjugates.forEach((row, t) =>
        row.forEach((c, k) => {
          const kk = key(c)
          const before = seen.get(kk)

          if (before) {
            mirrorRepeats.push(`${al.order}: w^${t} r_${k} w^-${t} = w^${before[0]} r_${before[1]} w^-${before[0]}`)

            if (before[1] === k && t - before[0] === 1) {
              invariantMirrors++
            }
          } else {
            seen.set(kk, [t, k])
          }
        }),
      )
    }

    // ---- R1 on {3,4,3,4} ----
    const space = lazySpaceFactory('{3,4,3,4}')!()

    const wordOf = (c: number): number[] => {
      const a = space.address(c)

      return a === '' ? [] : a.split('.').map(Number)
    }

    const trackFor = (letters: readonly number[]): Track => {
      const cache = new Map<number, number[]>()

      return (start, t) => {
        let list = cache.get(start)

        if (!list) {
          list = [start]

          let word = wordOf(start)

          for (let s = 1; s <= ROUNDS; s++) {
            word = [...word, ...letters]
            list.push(space.fromAddress(word.join('.')))
          }

          cache.set(start, list)
        }

        return list[t]!
      }
    }

    const tracks = new Map<Order, { along: Track; against: Track }>(
      ORDERS.map(order => {
        const own = roundLetters(order)
        const other = [...own].reverse()

        return [order, { along: trackFor(own), against: trackFor(other) }]
      }),
    )
    const starts = spaceBall(space, START_RADIUS, 100_000)!.cells
    const hyperbolic = readCells({
      space,
      rules,
      starts,
      tracks: order => tracks.get(order)!,
      displacement: null,
    })

    // ---- R3: meetings on {3,4,3,4} ----
    const meetBall = spaceBall(space, MEET_RADIUS, 100_000)!.cells.filter(c => c !== 0)
    const tileMatrix = (c: number): string => key(product(wordOf(c).map(g => faces[g]!)))
    const meetingSummary = algebras.map(al => {
      const lookup = matrixMeetings(al)
      const counts = meetBall.map(y => (lookup.get(tileMatrix(y)) ?? []).length)
      const met = meetBall.filter((_, i) => counts[i]! > 0)
      // the rounds at which each met tile is paired, for the report
      const roundsOf = met.map(y => `${space.address(y)}@${(lookup.get(tileMatrix(y)) ?? []).join('/')}`)

      return { order: al.order, lookup, counts, met: met.length, roundsOf }
    })
    const checkBall = spaceBall(space, CHECK_RADIUS, 100_000)!.cells.filter(c => c !== 0)

    let steppedAgrees = true

    for (const m of meetingSummary) {
      for (const y of checkBall) {
        const stepped = steppedMeetings(space, 0, y, m.order).join(',')
        const matrix = (m.lookup.get(tileMatrix(y)) ?? []).join(',')

        if (stepped !== matrix) {
          steppedAgrees = false
        }
      }
    }

    // an off-origin anchor: a = s_0, partners a s_h, read the same counts as (1, s_h)
    const anchor = space.partner(0, 0)

    let anchorAgrees = true

    for (const order of ORDERS) {
      for (let h = 0; h < 24; h++) {
        const y = space.partner(h, anchor)
        const shifted = steppedMeetings(space, anchor, y, order).join(',')
        const origin = steppedMeetings(space, 0, space.partner(h, 0), order).join(',')

        if (shifted !== origin) {
          anchorAgrees = false
        }
      }
    }

    // ---- CONTROL D4 ----
    const d4 = lazySpaceFactory('{3,4,3,3}')!()
    const coords = (c: number): number[] => d4.address(c).split(',').map(Number)
    const d4Starts = spaceBall(d4, START_RADIUS, 100_000)!.cells
    const flat = readCells({
      space: d4,
      rules,
      starts: d4Starts,
      tracks: () => ({ along: null, against: null }),
      displacement: (a, b) => {
        const x = coords(a)
        const y = coords(b)

        return y.map((v, i) => v - x[i]!).join(',')
      },
    })
    const d4Displacements = new Set<string>()

    for (const order of ORDERS) {
      for (const s of d4Starts) {
        let c = s

        for (const g of roundColors(d4, order)) {
          c = d4.partner(g, c)
        }

        d4Displacements.add(`${order}:${coords(c).map((v, i) => v - coords(s)[i]!).join(',')}`)
      }
    }

    const d4Anchors = spaceBall(d4, 1, 1000)!.cells
    const d4Counts: number[] = []

    for (const order of ORDERS) {
      for (const a of d4Anchors) {
        const base = coords(a)
        const near = spaceBall(d4, MEET_RADIUS, 100_000)!.cells.map(c => {
          const x = coords(c)

          return d4.fromAddress(x.map((v, i) => v + base[i]!).join(','))
        })

        for (const y of near) {
          if (y !== a) {
            d4Counts.push(steppedMeetings(d4, a, y, order).length)
          }
        }
      }
    }

    // ---- CONTROL LEVEL 4 ----
    const ring = levelRing({ twoPower: LEVEL_TWO_POWER, odd: 1 })
    const quotient = quotientOfW(faces, ring)

    let wOrder = 0
    let quotientGates = false
    let quotientCells: CellReading[] = []

    const quotientCounts: number[] = []

    let quotientMatrixAgrees = false

    if (quotient.fits) {
      const one = reduceToLevel(identity(), ring).join(',')
      const wMod = reduceToLevel(forward.w, ring)

      let p = wMod

      for (let t = 1; t <= 1_000_000; t++) {
        if (p.join(',') === one) {
          wOrder = t
          break
        }

        p = levelProduct(p, wMod, ring)
      }

      const qs = quotientSpace(quotient)

      quotientGates = Array.from({ length: quotient.docks }, (_, c) => {
        const n = qs.neighbors(c)

        return (
          n.every((v, g) => v !== c && qs.partner(g, v) === c) &&
          new Set(n).size === 24
        )
      }).every(Boolean)

      const qStarts = Array.from({ length: quotient.docks }, (_, c) => c).filter(c => quotient.distance[c]! <= START_RADIUS)

      const qTrack = (letters: readonly number[]): Track => (start, t) => {
        let c = start

        for (let s = 0; s < t; s++) {
          for (const g of letters) {
            c = qs.partner(g, c)
          }
        }

        return c
      }

      quotientCells = readCells({
        space: qs,
        rules,
        starts: qStarts,
        tracks: order => ({
          along: qTrack(roundLetters(order)),
          against: qTrack([...roundLetters(order)].reverse()),
        }),
        displacement: null,
      })

      const qNear = Array.from({ length: quotient.docks }, (_, c) => c).filter(
        c => c !== 0 && quotient.distance[c]! <= MEET_RADIUS,
      )

      quotientMatrixAgrees = true

      for (const al of algebras) {
        const lookup = new Map<number, number[]>()

        for (let t = 1; t <= MEET_ROUNDS; t++) {
          for (const c of al.conjugates[t - 1]!) {
            const dock = quotient.indexOf.get(reduceToLevel(c, ring).join(','))

            if (dock === undefined) {
              quotientMatrixAgrees = false
              continue
            }

            const list = lookup.get(dock) ?? []

            if (list[list.length - 1] !== t) {
              list.push(t)
            }

            lookup.set(dock, list)
          }
        }

        for (const y of qNear) {
          const stepped = steppedMeetings(qs, 0, y, al.order)

          if (stepped.join(',') !== (lookup.get(y) ?? []).join(',')) {
            quotientMatrixAgrees = false
          }

          quotientCounts.push(stepped.length)
        }
      }
    }

    // ---- verdict ----
    const blindAgrees = (cells: readonly CellReading[], wIsOne = false): boolean =>
      cells.every(
        c =>
          c.read === 'live background' ||
          c.predicted === null ||
          c.predicted === c.read ||
          // x w^t = x at every round end when w = 1, so a translated tone reads frozen there
          (wIsOne && c.predicted === 'translated' && c.read === 'frozen'),
      )
    const quotientBlind = blindAgrees(quotientCells, wOrder === 1)
    const flatBlindAgrees = flat.every(
      c => c.read === 'live background' || c.predicted === null || c.read === c.predicted,
    )
    const hyperbolicAgrees = hyperbolic.every(c => c.agrees)
    const tally = (cells: readonly CellReading[], cls: CellClass): number => cells.filter(c => c.read === cls).length
    const hCounts = meetingSummary.flatMap(m => m.counts)
    const maxHyperbolic = Math.max(...hCounts)
    const maxFlat = Math.max(...d4Counts)
    const persistentFlat = d4Counts.filter(c => c === MEET_ROUNDS).length
    const maxQuotient = quotientCounts.length > 0 ? Math.max(...quotientCounts) : 0
    const recurringQuotient = quotientCounts.filter(c => c >= 2).length
    const gates =
      census.rules.length === 24 &&
      involutions &&
      facesPreserve &&
      commutationAgrees &&
      infinitePairsAgree &&
      wPreserves &&
      wInverseAgrees &&
      loxodromic &&
      noPowerIsOne &&
      conjugatesAreReflections &&
      hyperbolicAgrees &&
      blindAgrees(hyperbolic) &&
      flatBlindAgrees &&
      steppedAgrees &&
      anchorAgrees &&
      quotient.fits &&
      quotientGates &&
      quotientMatrixAgrees &&
      quotientBlind
    const table = hyperbolic
      .map(c => `${c.rule} b${c.background} x${c.tone} ${c.order[0]}: ${c.read}`)
      .join('; ')

    return verdict({
      status: gates ? 'pass' : 'fail',
      claim: gates
        ? `on {3,4,3,4} every orientation-blind lone tone is frozen or moves x -> x w (x w^-1 reversed) from all ${starts.length} starts, with w = s_0 ... s_23 loxodromic (trace ${wTrace[0]} + ${wTrace[1]} sqrt 2); ${mirrorRepeats.length} coincidences among the ${(MIRROR_POWERS + 1) * 24} mirror conjugates per order (${invariantMirrors} w-invariant mirrors); of the ${meetBall.length} tiles within distance ${MEET_RADIUS}, ${meetingSummary.map(m => `${m.met} (${m.order})`).join(' and ')} are ever paired with the origin to round ${MEET_ROUNDS}, at most ${maxHyperbolic} rounds each; on flat D4 (the round a translation per parity class) the ${d4Counts.length} near pairs are paired at most ${maxFlat} rounds each too (${persistentFlat} in every round), so finitely many meetings is not a curvature effect; on the level-4 quotient (w of order ${wOrder}) ${recurringQuotient} of ${quotientCounts.length} near pairs meet in two or more rounds (at most ${maxQuotient})`
        : 'a gate failed: the representation, the round element, a predicted orientation-blind cell, the stepped meeting count or the quotient disagrees with the model (see control)',
      metrics: {
        rules: census.rules.length,
        starts: starts.length,
        cellsRead: hyperbolic.length,
        frozen: tally(hyperbolic, 'frozen'),
        translated: tally(hyperbolic, 'translated'),
        counterTranslated: tally(hyperbolic, 'counter'),
        orientationDependent: tally(hyperbolic, 'orientation-dependent'),
        other: tally(hyperbolic, 'other'),
        liveBackground: tally(hyperbolic, 'live background'),
        mirrorCoincidences: mirrorRepeats.length,
        invariantMirrors,
        meetTiles: meetBall.length,
        metForward: meetingSummary[0]!.met,
        metReverse: meetingSummary[1]!.met,
        maxMeetingsHyperbolic: maxHyperbolic,
        flatPairs: d4Counts.length,
        flatPersistentPairs: persistentFlat,
        maxMeetingsFlat: maxFlat,
        flatTranslated: tally(flat, 'translated'),
        flatOrientationDependent: tally(flat, 'orientation-dependent'),
        flatDisplacements: d4Displacements.size,
        quotientDocks: quotient.docks,
        quotientCoxeterOrder: wOrder,
        quotientPairs: quotientCounts.length,
        quotientRecurringPairs: recurringQuotient,
        maxMeetingsQuotient: maxQuotient,
        quotientTranslated: tally(quotientCells, 'translated'),
        quotientOrientationDependent: tally(quotientCells, 'orientation-dependent'),
      },
      control: {
        involutions: involutions ? 1 : 0,
        facesPreserveForm: facesPreserve ? 1 : 0,
        commutationAgrees: commutationAgrees ? 1 : 0,
        infinitePairsAgree: infinitePairsAgree ? 1 : 0,
        wPreservesForm: wPreserves ? 1 : 0,
        reversedRoundIsInverse: wInverseAgrees ? 1 : 0,
        loxodromic: loxodromic ? 1 : 0,
        noPowerIsOne: noPowerIsOne ? 1 : 0,
        conjugatesAreReflections: conjugatesAreReflections ? 1 : 0,
        hyperbolicPredictionAgrees: hyperbolicAgrees ? 1 : 0,
        flatBlindAgrees: flatBlindAgrees ? 1 : 0,
        steppedAgreesWithMatrix: steppedAgrees ? 1 : 0,
        offOriginAnchorAgrees: anchorAgrees ? 1 : 0,
        quotientFits: quotient.fits ? 1 : 0,
        quotientGraphGates: quotientGates ? 1 : 0,
        quotientMatrixAgrees: quotientMatrixAgrees ? 1 : 0,
        quotientBlindAgrees: quotientBlind ? 1 : 0,
      },
      notes: `L1, exact. The finiteness of meetings past round ${MEET_ROUNDS} is not shown here: it needs the orbit argument in Lean. Hyperbolic meeting counts per tile (count:tiles): ${meetingSummary.map(m => `${m.order} ${histogram(m.counts)}`).join('; ')}. Met tiles (address@rounds): ${meetingSummary.map(m => `${m.order} ${m.roundsOf.join(' ')}`).join('; ')}. Mirror coincidences: ${mirrorRepeats.slice(0, 40).join('; ') || 'none'}. D4 meeting counts (count:pairs): ${histogram(d4Counts)}; displacements per round: ${[...d4Displacements].join(' ')}. Level-4 quotient: ${quotient.docks} docks, w of order ${wOrder}, meeting counts ${histogram(quotientCounts)}. Cells on {3,4,3,4} (rule, background, tone, order): ${table}.`,
    })
  },
})
